                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A cute well crafted game.\r\n\r\nCat Quest begins with the hero looking for her lost sister in a big island inhabited by cats. You are quickly identified as someone with special powers and get ongoing on small quests. It's a 2d action game with emphasis on heavy combat.\r\n\r\nEvery enemy and boss works the same, they telegraph their attacks with different red shapes, giving you enough time to roll out or dodge the move. There's small and big chests that help with upgrading your equipment, there's basically weapons, armor and hats. You also have access to a variety of spells that can be upgraded by spending gold.\r\n\r\nSince the start you have access to practically the whole map, only blocked from areas that need special skills like water walk or fly. There's also a ton of side quests all over the world to help with leveling up. The main quest is actually quite short, and can be finished in less than one hour if you know how to prepare yourself. There's also dungeons that are generally optional as well, you can even dodge most enemies and just get the loot if you are too overpowered.\r\n\r\nTechnically, the graphics and setting work perfectly. It's a very well designed game and it stands out. The plot even has some surprising turns but for the most part, it's a world filled with generic random characters.\r\n\r\nIt's highly repetitive, and it works well for one full run. Getting the NG+ achievements is just a chore, with self imposed extra difficulty without any real extra content. Recommended for a light and casual gaming experience.",
